<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xu Shouhui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1360</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xu Shouhui was a leader of the southern Red Turban rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. In 1351 he proclaimed the Tianwan regime on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>, but power passed to his officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a>, who murdered him in 1360 and founded the Chen Han state, prompting commanders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-yuzhen">Ming Yuzhen</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> to break away.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xu-shouhui.jpg" alt="Xu Shouhui" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Turban.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
